    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and an integer XXX. The weirdness of a contiguous subsequence Al,Al+1,…,ArA_l, A_{l+1}, \\ldots, A_rAl​,Al+1​,…,Ar​ is defined as W(l,r)=∑i=lrAi⋅Xi−lW(l, r) = \\sum_{i=l}^r A_i \\cdot X^{i-l}W(l,r)=∑i=lr​Ai​⋅Xi−l. Find P=∏i=1N∏j=iNW(i,j)2P = \\prod_{i=1}^N \\prod_{j=i}^N W(i, j)^2P=∏i=1N​∏j=iN​W(i,j)2 modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0&lt;X&lt;998,244,3530 \\lt X \\lt 998,244,3530&lt;X&lt;998,244,353",
      "0≤Ai&lt;998,244,3530 \\le A_i \\lt 998,244,3530≤Ai​&lt;998,244,353 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (15 points):** A1=A2=…=ANA_1 = A_2 = \\ldots = A_NA1​=A2​=…=AN​"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and XXX.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
